.TH LIBMPQ__UPDATE_REMOVE_IDENTITY 3 2026-11-05 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__update_remove_identity \- remove one exact staged MPQ identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__update_remove_identity("
.BI "        mpq_update_s *" "update,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename,"
.BI "        uint16_t " "locale,"
.BI "        uint16_t " "platform"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Selects the exact filename, locale and platform in the current transaction
stage, including preceding successful operations. There is no neutral-locale
fallback. Existing name-based update functions retain their own behavior.
.PP
Classic-only archives support shared payload aliases. Replacement detaches
only the selected identity into a new payload; removal retains the old
payload until its last alias disappears; rename preserves other aliases.
Locale/platform values and applicable attributes and timestamps are retained.
Encrypted renames use the new basename and final FIX_KEY offset.
.PP
Mixed classic/HET/BET targets require consistent one-to-one identities and
complete extended hashes. Mutations that split a shared BET identity or lose
another identity are rejected. Unique HET/BET-only targets accept only zero
locale and platform. Unknown unrelated members retain packed bytes and
identities. Extended tables are never discarded to permit an operation.
.PP
These operations use transactional reconstruction. Embedded archives and
unrecognized trailers are unsupported on this path. Existing archive
version, v4 raw-chunk policy and supported metadata are preserved. Special
members and unsupported metadata or storage layouts are rejected.
.PP
A rejected operation leaves the preceding valid stage available. The original
archive remains unchanged until commit publishes a finalized working copy.
Commit and abort consume the update handle, including on error.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST reports a missing identity or invalid required argument.
For rename it also reports an occupied destination identity.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT reports ambiguous or unsupported metadata, inconsistent
mappings, or mismatched replacement options. Size, allocation, read, write,
seek and close errors use existing LIBMPQ_ERROR_* values.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__file_identity (3),
.BR libmpq__update_begin (3),
.BR libmpq__update_commit (3),
.BR libmpq__update_abort (3)
